      "next_deadline": "Requested with the land use application; Planning and Building reviews affordable housing plans before Planning Commission and Board approval.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "unclear",
      "layering_notes": "San Benito County is a small non-entitlement county with no housing department: the Resource Management Agency (Planning and Building, Abraham Prado, (831) 637-5313) administers the inclusionary ordinance, in-lieu fees, density bonus and TEFRA hearings; the Health and Human Services Agency (Community Services and Workforce Development) runs HHAP, the shelter and the Migrant Center; Behavioral Health holds BHSA; and the Housing Authority of the County of Santa Cruz administers vouchers and PBVs for Hollister and San Juan Bautista. The County has no HOME or CDBG entitlement, no housing trust fund NOFA and no County loan program; Hollister runs its own PLHA and CDBG programs (Pass 3). sanbenitocountyca.gov and the amlegal code library block automated access, so records were built from Board of Supervisors packets on cosb.granicus.com (attachments on d2kbkoa27fdvtw.cloudfront.net), HCD allocation tables and hacosantacruz.org. The County applies state law without local enhancements; the certified Housing Element and Residential High rezoning are the main 2026 change, opening higher-density sites near Hollister for 100% affordable projects that can also use the state density bonus. Source is the December 13, 2022 Board packet; Housing Element approval details from the January 13 and February 10, 2026 agendas on cosb.granicus.com.",
